subproblem.statement:
Let n, l be natural numbers, r a real number, and f : R^n -> R^l (Rn n -> Rn l) 1-Lipschitz on the closed ball closedBall 0 r. Write |Df(x)|^2 := hsNormSq(fderiv R f x) = sum_{i<n} ||Df(x) e_i||^2 with e_i = EuclideanSpace.single i 1. Write f^j(y) := (f y)_j for j in Fin l, and grad f^j := gradient f^j. These are Mathlib's fderiv and gradient, which are 0 where the map is not differentiable. Then:
(a) x -> |Df(x)|^2 is measurable and, for every j, grad f^j is measurable;
(b) |Df(x)|^2 >= 0 for every x;
(c) for every x in the open ball ball 0 r: |Df(x)|^2 <= n, and ||grad f^j(x)|| <= 1 for every j;
(d) for Lebesgue-a.e. x in R^n: if x is in ball 0 r, then ||grad f^j(x)||^2 <= |Df(x)|^2 for every j.
